  "issue_title": "Add a network-wide weight-setting activity chart to /leaderboards",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\nThe issue's own body: \"GET /api/v1/chain/weights \u2014 live network-wide weight-setting activity, unconsumed.\" That route is real and live: `src/chain-weights.mjs` computes it from the `account_events` `WeightsSet` stream (registered in `src/contracts.mjs:2988-3001` as `chain-weights`, 7d/30d window, `limit` up to 100, CSV export supported). Nothing in `apps/ui/src` calls it today \u2014 there is no `chainWeightsQuery` in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts`, and no `/leaderboards` route exists yet in `apps/ui/src/routes/` (confirmed against `apps/ui/src/routeTree.gen.ts`). This is one of five sibling issues (#3465, #3466, #3469, #3470, #3473) that together stand up that new page \u2014 whichever of these five lands first creates the route shell; the rest extend it.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a `/leaderboards` route (create it if it doesn't yet exist when this PR lands) with a section rendering the network-wide weight-setting activity: the per-subnet leaderboard ranked by `weight_sets`, the network rollup (distinct setters, total weight-sets), and the intensity-distribution summary, all sourced live from `GET /api/v1/chain/weights`.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/weights` (registered `src/contracts.mjs:2988-3001`; builder `src/chain-weights.mjs` \u2014 `loadChainWeights`/`buildChainWeights`; params `window` (`7d`|`30d`, default `7d`) and `limit` (default 20, max 100); supports `?format=csv` for the per-subnet leaderboard)\n- Query function: **none exists.** Verified no `chainWeightsQuery` (or equivalent) anywhere in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` or `types.ts`. This PR must add both the typed query function AND the UI wiring in one PR \u2014 a data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n  - Add a `ChainWeights` type to `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` matching the builder's real output shape (`src/chain-weights.mjs:110-196`): `schema_version`, `window`, `observed_at`, `subnet_count`, `network: { distinct_setters, weight_sets, sets_per_setter }`, `intensity_distribution: { count, mean, min, p25, median, p75, p90, max } | null`, `subnets: Array<{ netuid, distinct_setters, weight_sets, sets_per_setter }>`.\n  - Add `chainWeightsQuery(window = \"7d\", limit = 20)` to `queries.ts` following the existing `chainTransferPairsQuery` pattern (`apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts:2439-2458`): `queryOptions` + `apiFetch<Partial<ChainWeights>>(\"/api/v1/chain/weights\", { params: { window, limit }, signal })` + a `normalizeChainWeights` normalizer (mirror `normalizeSubnetWeights` at `queries.ts:3222-3233` for per-field coercion) + `staleTime: STALE_MED`.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File(s) to change: `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` (new `ChainWeights` type), `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (new `normalizeChainWeights` + `chainWeightsQuery`), and a new `apps/ui/src/routes/leaderboards.tsx` (or, if a sibling PR from #3465/#3466/#3470/#3473 has already landed by the time this one is worked, extend that existing route file instead of re-creating it \u2014 check `apps/ui/src/routes/` first).\n- Exact anchor: there is no existing `/leaderboards` route to extend as of this repo state \u2014 this PR (or whichever sibling lands first) creates `apps/ui/src/routes/leaderboards.tsx` as a TanStack Router route file, following the shape of an existing simple index route (e.g. `apps/ui/src/routes/blocks.index.tsx` or `apps/ui/src/routes/providers.index.tsx`) for loader/error-boundary conventions.\n- What to render: a leaderboard section \u2014 a small `StatTile`-style row for the network rollup (distinct setters, total weight-sets, sets-per-setter) plus a ranked table/list of `subnets[]` (rank, netuid + subnet name/icon via `BrandIcon` linking to `/subnets/$netuid` \u2014 same link pattern as `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx:101-129`), each row showing `distinct_setters`, `weight_sets`, and `sets_per_setter`. Do not confuse this with the existing `leaderboards.tsx` component/`leaderboardsQuery` (registry health/completeness boards from `/api/v1/registry/leaderboards`, #1111) \u2014 that is a separate, already-shipped homepage module; this issue's leaderboard is a new section on the new `/leaderboards` route, keyed to a different endpoint entirely.\n- Coordination note: four sibling issues target the same new `/leaderboards` route \u2014 #3465 (registrations), #3466 (deregistrations), #3470 (\"twin of the route above\": `/api/v1/chain/weights/setters`, the validator-level leaderboard), and #3473 (turnover/volatility). Whichever PR lands first should create the route shell others can extend; if a sibling's PR merges first, rebase onto its route file rather than re-creating it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] The component/route imports and calls `chainWeightsQuery` via `useQuery`/`useSuspenseQuery`\n- [ ] Renders the network rollup (`network.distinct_setters`, `network.weight_sets`, `network.sets_per_setter`) and the ranked per-subnet list (`subnets[]`, each linking to its subnet detail page via `netuid`)\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states handled, matching the pattern already used in the target route file (or, if creating the route fresh, the null-on-error/empty-hides pattern used by `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/leaderboards.tsx:54-61`)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not touch the existing `leaderboards.tsx` component or `leaderboardsQuery` (registry completeness/health boards, #1111) \u2014 that is a separate, already-shipped feature on a different endpoint.\n- Do not implement the validator-level weight-setters leaderboard (`/api/v1/chain/weights/setters`) here \u2014 that is #3470's scope.\n- Do not implement the registrations/deregistrations/turnover leaderboards here \u2014 those are #3465/#3466/#3473's scope.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
